    "result": "`compare_versions` is implemented in `solution.py`, and all 37 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I didn't run a coverage check, so the 90% gate is unconfirmed. The function has few branches, and the tests exercise all of them.\n\nA single regex validates the format, including no leading zeros on numeric parts and `ValueError` for malformed input. Precedence then follows the spec's order: numeric major/minor/patch, then a release over a prerelease, then prerelease identifiers left to right, with build metadata ignored. Non-string input also raises `ValueError`, which the spec doesn't mention.\n\nThe tests cover ordering cases, symmetry (swapping the arguments flips the result), build-metadata equality and a range of invalid strings.",
